1
00:00:04,963 --> 00:00:06,089
♪

2
00:00:07,424 --> 00:00:08,634
[Nitobe gasps softly]

3
00:00:08,717 --> 00:00:10,636
What did you just do?

4
00:00:12,262 --> 00:00:13,388
I'm bleeding.

5
00:00:14,181 --> 00:00:15,515
Oh, it hurts.

6
00:00:16,308 --> 00:00:18,810
It hurts so much
I could just die!

7
00:00:18,894 --> 00:00:20,103
-[Satoko gasps]
-[whimpers]

8
00:00:20,187 --> 00:00:22,856
I won't though, don't worry,
Satoko.

9
00:00:22,940 --> 00:00:25,484
Even if he shoots
my body full of holes,

10
00:00:25,567 --> 00:00:27,236
I will still save you,

11
00:00:27,319 --> 00:00:29,863
just as any good husband should.

12
00:00:31,073 --> 00:00:33,283
[♪ opening theme song playing]

13
00:02:01,997 --> 00:02:03,623
I walked out of the room
when you told me to,

14
00:02:03,707 --> 00:02:05,250
and I waited patiently.

15
00:02:05,334 --> 00:02:07,669
I had to resist the urge
to come back inside.

16
00:02:08,337 --> 00:02:10,714
That is, until I heard you
make up your mind.

17
00:02:10,797 --> 00:02:13,633
Stay away! Take one more step
and I swear this woman's--

18
00:02:13,717 --> 00:02:16,136
In my eyes, anyone who lays
a hand on my wife

19
00:02:16,219 --> 00:02:18,305
deserves to be cut down
without question.

20
00:02:18,388 --> 00:02:21,016
But if you tell me you'd rather
keep him alive, Satoko,

21
00:02:21,099 --> 00:02:22,434
I'll do as you say.

22
00:02:24,061 --> 00:02:27,439
Everything...
everything I do is for you.

23
00:02:27,522 --> 00:02:30,650
What's wrong with him?
He's giving me the creeps!

24
00:02:30,942 --> 00:02:32,194
Go away!

25
00:02:32,736 --> 00:02:34,780
[gasps] Get back here, bitch!

26
00:02:34,863 --> 00:02:36,823
[grunting]

27
00:02:49,002 --> 00:02:50,128
[Satoko gasps softly]

28
00:02:51,880 --> 00:02:54,299
That's more than enough.
He's not even conscious--

29
00:02:54,383 --> 00:02:56,176
This isn't nearly enough yet.

30
00:02:56,259 --> 00:02:59,054
I need to make sure he's sorry
for what he did to you.

31
00:02:59,137 --> 00:03:01,515
-Yes, but how can he--
-[thumping]

32
00:03:01,598 --> 00:03:03,392
Pardon,
but are you even listening?

33
00:03:04,393 --> 00:03:05,602
[gasps]

34
00:03:05,685 --> 00:03:07,854
[thumping continues]

35
00:03:10,399 --> 00:03:11,650
[Satoko grunts]

36
00:03:14,111 --> 00:03:15,904
[Satoko panting]

37
00:03:15,987 --> 00:03:17,948
Didn't you hear me? I said stop.

38
00:03:20,033 --> 00:03:21,118
[screams]

39
00:03:21,410 --> 00:03:23,662
I'm sorry. I didn't mean it.
I got carried away.

40
00:03:23,745 --> 00:03:26,540
Oh, Satoko,
look at how I'm bleeding.

41
00:03:28,417 --> 00:03:29,918
Wipe it off for me.

42
00:03:30,001 --> 00:03:32,337
Use a soft handkerchief, please.

43
00:03:32,421 --> 00:03:34,131
[SATOKO]
The gunshot wound comes first.

44
00:03:34,214 --> 00:03:37,801
[SHINPEI] Forget about that,
just wipe my forehead gently.

45
00:03:37,884 --> 00:03:40,178
[cloth rustling]

46
00:03:40,262 --> 00:03:41,555
[Shinpei chuckles softly]

47
00:03:43,724 --> 00:03:44,725
It seems...

48
00:03:45,308 --> 00:03:48,145
I do owe you my thanks.
You have saved me once again.

49
00:03:48,228 --> 00:03:49,312
[SHINPEI] Mm?

50
00:03:50,105 --> 00:03:51,356
I did?

51
00:03:51,440 --> 00:03:53,358
Then have you fallen
even more in love with me?

52
00:03:53,442 --> 00:03:54,693
No, I have not.

53
00:03:55,819 --> 00:03:57,737
-[Shinpei gasps]
-Let me explain.

54
00:03:57,821 --> 00:04:01,241
I don't appreciate the way
you take everything too far.

55
00:04:01,324 --> 00:04:04,244
If you're trying to impress me,
that is not how you'll do it.

56
00:04:04,327 --> 00:04:05,370
[SHINPEI] Hmm?

57
00:04:05,745 --> 00:04:07,539
Given your line of work,
perhaps you don't know,

58
00:04:07,622 --> 00:04:09,416
but violence is wrong.

59
00:04:09,499 --> 00:04:12,419
To punch someone like that
is completely barbaric.

60
00:04:12,878 --> 00:04:14,337
Let me be clear.

61
00:04:14,421 --> 00:04:17,507
No matter whose life it is,
you must never take it.

62
00:04:18,467 --> 00:04:20,552
But isn't it violent
to hit someone with a lantern--

63
00:04:20,635 --> 00:04:21,803
And another thing!

64
00:04:22,554 --> 00:04:25,307
You've been shot,
you shouldn't be moving around.

65
00:04:25,765 --> 00:04:27,225
You're still bleeding.

66
00:04:27,309 --> 00:04:29,561
Probably because
you won't stay still.

67
00:04:30,604 --> 00:04:31,730
If you were to die,

68
00:04:31,813 --> 00:04:34,149
what do you expect me to do
with myself?

69
00:04:34,816 --> 00:04:36,318
[Shinpei gasps softly]

70
00:04:36,985 --> 00:04:39,321
You really don't want me to die?

71
00:04:39,404 --> 00:04:41,114
I refuse to answer that.

72
00:04:42,115 --> 00:04:44,826
[SHINPEI] This is not exactly
how I thought this would go.

73
00:04:44,910 --> 00:04:46,828
I'm going to go
call for someone.

74
00:04:46,912 --> 00:04:48,246
You lie down until then.

75
00:04:50,791 --> 00:04:53,585
I'm dreadfully sorry
for my behavior back there.

76
00:04:53,668 --> 00:04:55,962
I never dreamed
I would do something so vulgar

77
00:04:56,046 --> 00:04:57,255
while I was drunk.

78
00:04:57,589 --> 00:04:59,633
I don't know
how to make it up to you.

79
00:04:59,716 --> 00:05:02,844
In that case,
would you do me this one favor?

80
00:05:02,928 --> 00:05:04,054
Anything you ask.

81
00:05:04,679 --> 00:05:07,682
All right.
Take a message to my family.

82
00:05:08,266 --> 00:05:09,684
Tell the Kirigayas,

83
00:05:09,768 --> 00:05:12,270
although she's held captive
on an island,

84
00:05:12,354 --> 00:05:14,564
Satoko will make it home alive.

85
00:05:14,648 --> 00:05:15,982
They'll get your message.

86
00:05:16,066 --> 00:05:17,692
I can promise you that much.

87
00:05:18,193 --> 00:05:21,738
And you, I really am sorry
about the gunshot.

88
00:05:22,239 --> 00:05:24,074
If anything like this
happens again,

89
00:05:24,157 --> 00:05:26,368
I won't hesitate
to end your life.

90
00:05:26,451 --> 00:05:28,453
We thank you
for your continued patronage.

91
00:05:28,537 --> 00:05:30,205
[screaming]

92
00:05:30,288 --> 00:05:32,207
I swear that
I'll deliver your message.

93
00:05:32,290 --> 00:05:34,376
-[SATOKO] Uh?
-[NITOBE] Goodbye!

94
00:05:35,001 --> 00:05:37,045
Please, come again soon!

95
00:05:37,128 --> 00:05:38,380
I'm so sorry.

96
00:05:38,463 --> 00:05:40,423
-Hmm?
-You were hurt,

97
00:05:40,507 --> 00:05:42,509
and it's because
I couldn't handle things.

98
00:05:42,592 --> 00:05:44,719
Don't worry,
I'm used to being shot!

99
00:05:44,803 --> 00:05:46,721
-Huh?
-Actually...

100
00:05:46,805 --> 00:05:47,889
I'm more concerned with

101
00:05:47,973 --> 00:05:49,975
how his cup
was filled with sake.

102
00:05:50,392 --> 00:05:52,519
Seems someone decided
to play a prank.

103
00:05:53,395 --> 00:05:55,814
-Hmm.
-What about you, Satoko?

104
00:05:56,481 --> 00:05:58,066
He treated you rather rough.

105
00:05:58,149 --> 00:05:59,776
Does your scar hurt
after all that?

106
00:06:00,402 --> 00:06:02,320
Oh. My scar?

107
00:06:03,280 --> 00:06:06,700
That's right. I wonder
how much he overheard.

108
00:06:07,117 --> 00:06:09,369
Or worse,
did he actually see it?

109
00:06:09,452 --> 00:06:10,787
-Satoko.
-Uh?

110
00:06:12,455 --> 00:06:13,498
[screams]

111
00:06:14,124 --> 00:06:15,458
Why are you half-naked?

112
00:06:15,542 --> 00:06:17,002
Look at my scars.

113
00:06:17,085 --> 00:06:18,003
Uh?

114
00:06:18,086 --> 00:06:19,879
If you compare yours to mine,

115
00:06:19,963 --> 00:06:22,507
I don't think yours is even
worth worrying about.

116
00:06:22,591 --> 00:06:23,717
♪

117
00:06:24,593 --> 00:06:25,760
[chuckles]

118
00:06:27,512 --> 00:06:31,057
[SATOKO] He must be saying this
to cheer me up in his own way.

119
00:06:32,309 --> 00:06:35,729
Since I was little,
I've tried my best to hide it.

120
00:06:35,812 --> 00:06:39,065
But this man, he makes me...

121
00:06:39,691 --> 00:06:41,985
I'll have you know
my scar is far bigger

122
00:06:42,068 --> 00:06:43,820
and deeper
than any that you have.

123
00:06:44,988 --> 00:06:46,406
Quite impressive, no?

124
00:06:46,489 --> 00:06:48,491
It's my badge of honor.

125
00:06:48,575 --> 00:06:51,453
He makes me want
to bare myself to him.

126
00:06:53,705 --> 00:06:54,998
[Shinpei chuckles softly]

127
00:06:55,081 --> 00:06:56,833
But you'll still
never come close

128
00:06:56,916 --> 00:06:57,959
to how many I have.

129
00:06:58,376 --> 00:07:01,296
There's no need to make it
a competition. [coughs]

130
00:07:01,379 --> 00:07:02,672
More importantly,

131
00:07:02,756 --> 00:07:05,050
now we have to find another way
off this island.

132
00:07:05,133 --> 00:07:07,218
Ah, you raise a worthy point.

133
00:07:07,844 --> 00:07:09,220
If we ask around the island,

134
00:07:09,304 --> 00:07:11,556
then we might get ideas.
[coughing]

135
00:07:11,640 --> 00:07:14,476
We'll draw suspicion
if we move around. Hm?

136
00:07:14,559 --> 00:07:15,602
[continues coughing]

137
00:07:15,685 --> 00:07:17,312
Are you sure you feel all right?

138
00:07:17,896 --> 00:07:21,816
[Satoko coughing] I'm sorry.
Once I start, I can't stop.

139
00:07:23,068 --> 00:07:24,069
[sputters]

140
00:07:26,321 --> 00:07:27,947
Is that...

141
00:07:29,199 --> 00:07:30,367
Satoko!

142
00:07:33,370 --> 00:07:35,413
[singing] ♪ Tell us all,
where did you go? ♪

143
00:07:35,497 --> 00:07:38,500
♪ To Higo
Where in Higo? ♪

144
00:07:38,583 --> 00:07:42,045
♪ To Kumamoto
Where in Kumamoto? ♪

145
00:07:43,588 --> 00:07:44,798
[SATOKO] Mother!

146
00:07:45,840 --> 00:07:47,759
May I go outside
with the other children

147
00:07:47,842 --> 00:07:48,802
for just a while?

148
00:07:48,885 --> 00:07:51,096
Don't be ridiculous,
of course not.

149
00:07:51,179 --> 00:07:53,682
It's barely been three days
since your fever came down.

150
00:07:53,765 --> 00:07:56,101
I'll only watch Miwako
and her friends.

151
00:07:56,184 --> 00:07:58,603
I promise I won't join
in their games.

152
00:07:58,687 --> 00:08:02,440
[sighs] Satoko, you clearly
don't understand

153
00:08:02,524 --> 00:08:04,192
why you were born, do you?

154
00:08:04,734 --> 00:08:07,570
You are the property
of the Kirigaya family.

155
00:08:07,654 --> 00:08:09,322
In other words, just a tool.

156
00:08:09,948 --> 00:08:12,867
Even at your best,
you're a burden on us.

157
00:08:12,951 --> 00:08:15,578
The least you can do
is carry out your role.

158
00:08:15,662 --> 00:08:18,790
Don't imagine
you have any freedom.

159
00:08:19,708 --> 00:08:20,917
[SHINPEI] Satoko...

160
00:08:21,584 --> 00:08:22,502
Satoko.

161
00:08:22,585 --> 00:08:23,795
[gasps]

162
00:08:23,878 --> 00:08:25,463
Ah, you're awake.

163
00:08:26,339 --> 00:08:27,507
How are you?

164
00:08:28,091 --> 00:08:31,094
Uh, where are we?

165
00:08:31,177 --> 00:08:32,846
A room at Isekichi.

166
00:08:33,471 --> 00:08:35,598
You collapsed,
so I carried you inside.

167
00:08:36,850 --> 00:08:38,560
[SATOKO] It happened again.

168
00:08:38,643 --> 00:08:39,978
[SHINPEI] Thank goodness.

169
00:08:40,061 --> 00:08:41,438
I was so worried.

170
00:08:41,521 --> 00:08:43,148
You've been asleep
for three whole days now!

171
00:08:43,231 --> 00:08:44,816
Three whole days?

172
00:08:45,275 --> 00:08:47,527
You had to watch me. I'm sorry.

173
00:08:47,610 --> 00:08:48,862
No, it's all right.

174
00:08:48,945 --> 00:08:50,530
It's a husband's responsibility

175
00:08:50,613 --> 00:08:52,115
to take care of his wife
when she's sick.

176
00:08:52,198 --> 00:08:53,450
That being said,

177
00:08:53,533 --> 00:08:55,744
it didn't seem like
you were sleeping very well.

178
00:08:55,827 --> 00:08:57,746
-Did you have nightmares?
-Uh?

179
00:08:59,497 --> 00:09:02,459
I was dreaming about
my childhood, nothing else.

180
00:09:03,418 --> 00:09:06,671
Back then, I was even more frail
than I am now.

181
00:09:07,338 --> 00:09:08,673
And when I fell ill,

182
00:09:08,757 --> 00:09:10,759
I wasn't allowed
out of the house for some time,

183
00:09:10,842 --> 00:09:12,385
even after I felt better.

184
00:09:13,595 --> 00:09:16,055
The thought occurred
that I might die in that room,

185
00:09:16,139 --> 00:09:18,892
with no one else around.
I was terrified.

186
00:09:20,059 --> 00:09:21,102
[SHINPEI] Mm...

187
00:09:21,561 --> 00:09:23,146
Just one moment.

188
00:09:24,814 --> 00:09:25,857
[SATOKO] Mm?

189
00:09:27,484 --> 00:09:29,277
-[door slides open]
-[SHINPEI] I'm back.

190
00:09:29,360 --> 00:09:31,362
Sorry that took so long.

191
00:09:31,446 --> 00:09:33,072
I'm gonna put the light out
for a bit.

192
00:09:35,033 --> 00:09:36,326
[Satoko gasps softly]

193
00:09:36,409 --> 00:09:38,203
♪

194
00:09:42,165 --> 00:09:43,333
[exclaims softly]

195
00:09:43,416 --> 00:09:44,876
♪

196
00:09:48,171 --> 00:09:50,507
I caught them down by the river.

197
00:09:50,590 --> 00:09:52,926
Doesn't it make it feel
just like we're outside?

198
00:09:53,009 --> 00:09:54,302
[Satoko gasps softly]

199
00:09:57,138 --> 00:10:00,975
Wherever we go, I promise that
I'll always set you free.

200
00:10:01,059 --> 00:10:02,143
[SATOKO] Mm?

201
00:10:04,187 --> 00:10:06,147
Such an odd fellow.

202
00:10:06,231 --> 00:10:09,234
I've been scared of him
this whole time, and yet...

203
00:10:09,317 --> 00:10:10,527
You know what I heard?

204
00:10:11,820 --> 00:10:14,489
Fireflies spend most
of their lives in the water.

205
00:10:15,156 --> 00:10:17,075
Once they surface
and take to the air,

206
00:10:17,158 --> 00:10:18,785
they don't have
very much time left.

207
00:10:19,953 --> 00:10:22,247
Guess they glow all the brighter
while they're here.

208
00:10:23,331 --> 00:10:24,499
[sighs softly]

209
00:10:28,795 --> 00:10:31,130
Uh? Uh-oh, didn't feel well?

210
00:10:31,214 --> 00:10:32,882
♪

211
00:10:39,055 --> 00:10:40,390
-Listen.
-Hm?

212
00:10:40,473 --> 00:10:43,017
I really appreciate
the thoughtful gesture,

213
00:10:43,101 --> 00:10:44,853
but would you mind
if I let them out?

214
00:10:46,813 --> 00:10:48,940
If their lives are so short,

215
00:10:49,023 --> 00:10:51,192
then they shouldn't waste them
in here.

216
00:10:54,737 --> 00:10:57,156
I'd prefer to let the fireflies
shine their light

217
00:10:57,240 --> 00:10:58,783
wherever they please.

218
00:10:59,492 --> 00:11:00,535
[gasps softly]

219
00:11:00,618 --> 00:11:01,870
♪

220
00:11:05,498 --> 00:11:08,376
[chuckles]
You're a kind person, Satoko.

221
00:11:09,669 --> 00:11:12,505
I know. Once we get out of here,
let's build a house

222
00:11:12,589 --> 00:11:14,757
where we can see
the fireflies every summer!

223
00:11:14,841 --> 00:11:16,885
Somewhere close to a river
would be best.

224
00:11:16,968 --> 00:11:19,637
That way, we can go fishing,
and swim when it's hot out!

225
00:11:20,138 --> 00:11:22,849
I've never had the chance
to swim in a river before.

226
00:11:22,932 --> 00:11:24,392
What? Not even once?

227
00:11:24,475 --> 00:11:27,687
Although, I might enjoy it.

228
00:11:27,770 --> 00:11:29,856
Very well, then,
that settles things!

229
00:11:30,356 --> 00:11:32,400
I want to spend
all the time I can with you,

230
00:11:32,483 --> 00:11:34,903
-so maybe I'll work a bit less.
-Mm?

231
00:11:36,613 --> 00:11:38,448
I'm wondering
if you plan on working

232
00:11:38,531 --> 00:11:40,116
the rest of your life
as an assassin?

233
00:11:40,742 --> 00:11:43,328
Of course.
What am I if I'm not a killer?

234
00:11:43,411 --> 00:11:45,121
Then there would be
nothing left of me.

235
00:11:45,955 --> 00:11:49,083
Besides, I'll need money
to make you happy, right?

236
00:11:50,668 --> 00:11:52,879
Anytime I've heard you talk
about the future,

237
00:11:52,962 --> 00:11:54,589
it revolves around me.

238
00:11:54,672 --> 00:11:57,050
Isn't there anything that
you want for yourself?

239
00:11:57,759 --> 00:12:01,262
Are you so ready to forsake
your birthplace for marriage?

240
00:12:01,346 --> 00:12:04,098
I don't feel particularly
attached to this island.

241
00:12:04,182 --> 00:12:05,808
What of your parents?

242
00:12:05,892 --> 00:12:07,602
I never knew my father.

243
00:12:07,685 --> 00:12:09,896
My mother was a prostitute.

244
00:12:09,979 --> 00:12:13,149
A customer killed her
when I was young. Too young.

245
00:12:13,232 --> 00:12:15,568
But I never forgot
about that man,

246
00:12:15,652 --> 00:12:18,112
and I made him the first person
I ever killed.

247
00:12:19,113 --> 00:12:21,074
I still remember every detail...

248
00:12:21,699 --> 00:12:23,910
the way he writhed in agony.

249
00:12:23,993 --> 00:12:26,871
It was so incredible
to watch him die.

250
00:12:30,124 --> 00:12:32,126
Well, don't you feel sorry
for me?

251
00:12:32,210 --> 00:12:33,294
[SATOKO] Mm?

252
00:12:33,711 --> 00:12:36,130
Why don't you comfort me
and tell me it's all right?

253
00:12:36,214 --> 00:12:39,634
My existence is so very sad.
Waaah!

254
00:12:39,717 --> 00:12:42,220
Have you always made
these ridiculous jokes?

255
00:12:42,303 --> 00:12:44,138
Is it how you hide
from your feelings?

256
00:12:45,640 --> 00:12:46,641
[SHINPEI] Uh?

257
00:12:47,225 --> 00:12:49,811
I can tell you want
to escape this island,

258
00:12:49,894 --> 00:12:51,354
just like I do.

259
00:12:53,439 --> 00:12:55,608
Hiding it won't change reality.

260
00:12:56,317 --> 00:12:59,028
Running away
is a more positive approach.

261
00:13:00,989 --> 00:13:03,408
We should leave
this island together.

262
00:13:04,033 --> 00:13:05,660
We can both be free.

263
00:13:05,743 --> 00:13:06,828
[SHINPEI] Uh?

264
00:13:07,245 --> 00:13:08,246
[chuckles]

265
00:13:08,329 --> 00:13:10,415
You truly want to run away
with me?

266
00:13:10,498 --> 00:13:12,458
Mm? Yes.

267
00:13:12,834 --> 00:13:15,169
Only until I'm off this island.

268
00:13:15,253 --> 00:13:16,921
I'm so glad.

269
00:13:17,005 --> 00:13:19,298
Well, we'll need a new plan.

270
00:13:19,382 --> 00:13:21,551
Oh, no, they're loose now.

271
00:13:22,176 --> 00:13:24,178
It's such a pain to wrap them.

272
00:13:24,637 --> 00:13:25,805
[Satoko sighs]

273
00:13:26,222 --> 00:13:28,349
[Shinpei humming]

274
00:13:28,433 --> 00:13:31,352
I've constantly needed you
to protect me.

275
00:13:31,436 --> 00:13:33,896
I'm sorry this is all I can do
to repay you.

276
00:13:33,980 --> 00:13:35,940
What? Everything you do for me

277
00:13:36,024 --> 00:13:37,942
already makes me happier
than I can say.

278
00:13:38,026 --> 00:13:39,193
[Satoko gasps softly]

279
00:13:40,278 --> 00:13:42,613
[SATOKO] Being so helpless
is frustrating.

280
00:13:43,114 --> 00:13:45,783
He's willing to get hurt
just to stay near me.

281
00:13:46,242 --> 00:13:47,869
If I can't make myself useful,

282
00:13:47,952 --> 00:13:51,164
I'll just find myself a burden
to yet another person.

283
00:13:51,247 --> 00:13:52,915
There. Much better!

284
00:13:53,708 --> 00:13:55,376
-Thank you, Satoko.
-[gasps softly]

285
00:13:55,460 --> 00:13:57,712
This is for all the help!

286
00:13:58,171 --> 00:13:59,797
[Satoko squeals]

287
00:13:59,881 --> 00:14:01,090
-[Shinpei sighs]
-[gasps]

288
00:14:01,174 --> 00:14:02,759
What bliss...

289
00:14:03,468 --> 00:14:05,345
Just having you
by my side is enough.

290
00:14:06,763 --> 00:14:08,181
[Satoko gasps softly]

291
00:14:08,723 --> 00:14:10,308
-And up.
-[yelps]

292
00:14:10,391 --> 00:14:13,436
You're still healing,
so I'll carry you back to bed.

293
00:14:15,229 --> 00:14:16,272
All right.

294
00:14:17,065 --> 00:14:18,441
It's strange.

295
00:14:19,150 --> 00:14:22,111
I feel oddly self-conscious
around him.

296
00:14:23,071 --> 00:14:25,281
You sure are light, huh?

297
00:14:25,365 --> 00:14:26,991
I don't think so.

298
00:14:27,075 --> 00:14:28,701
Of all the girls
I've ever carried,

299
00:14:28,785 --> 00:14:30,495
-you're the lightest.
-Uh?

300
00:14:32,121 --> 00:14:33,539
I don't want to hear that.

301
00:14:33,623 --> 00:14:35,792
What? No one's minded it before.

302
00:14:35,875 --> 00:14:38,336
Women love it when I tell them
how light they are.

303
00:14:42,215 --> 00:14:43,925
Thank you for helping me.

304
00:14:45,093 --> 00:14:47,220
I guess you're used
to this sort of thing.

305
00:14:47,303 --> 00:14:48,262
Not really.

306
00:14:50,223 --> 00:14:53,976
Tell me,
your affections are clear,

307
00:14:54,060 --> 00:14:56,187
but what about me
appeals to you?

308
00:14:56,270 --> 00:14:57,688
Everything about you.

309
00:14:57,772 --> 00:14:59,899
But the fact
that you accepted me as I am

310
00:14:59,982 --> 00:15:00,942
is the best part.

311
00:15:01,025 --> 00:15:02,276
[Satoko gasps softly]

312
00:15:02,610 --> 00:15:05,780
Now I see why he agreed
to such a sudden marriage offer.

313
00:15:06,364 --> 00:15:09,450
He doesn't love me. He only...

314
00:15:10,326 --> 00:15:13,162
So, if any other girl would've
"accepted you as you are,"

315
00:15:13,246 --> 00:15:14,914
she would have done
just as well?

316
00:15:14,997 --> 00:15:15,998
Uh, hold on.

317
00:15:16,082 --> 00:15:17,583
I only want to marry you,
Satoko.

318
00:15:17,667 --> 00:15:19,627
You only met me a few days ago.

319
00:15:19,710 --> 00:15:21,546
How can you be so sure
you love me?

320
00:15:22,171 --> 00:15:25,716
Look at you. Can an assassin
even understand love?

321
00:15:26,092 --> 00:15:28,302
You don't love me
as a man loves a woman.

322
00:15:28,386 --> 00:15:30,096
You can't.
I'm sure that you love me

323
00:15:30,179 --> 00:15:31,639
like a child or a pet.

324
00:15:33,224 --> 00:15:35,059
I know I'm being unreasonable.

325
00:15:35,685 --> 00:15:38,062
Why bother
when I don't love him either?

326
00:15:38,479 --> 00:15:41,691
Well, if you're so sure,
do you really know what love is?

327
00:15:41,774 --> 00:15:42,733
[SATOKO] Mm?

328
00:15:43,276 --> 00:15:46,112
Uh, love is this feeling that...
that you...

329
00:15:46,195 --> 00:15:50,324
It's when two people care
for one another. Or well...

330
00:15:50,950 --> 00:15:52,994
It's something that
a pair nurtures together!

331
00:15:54,620 --> 00:15:55,663
[SHINPEI] Hm?

332
00:15:56,080 --> 00:15:58,291
[SATOKO] I can only describe it
in the abstract.

333
00:15:58,374 --> 00:15:59,333
In any case,

334
00:15:59,876 --> 00:16:01,836
I wish you wouldn't talk
about marrying me so lightly.

335
00:16:01,919 --> 00:16:04,130
I don't understand.
Why are you so angry?

336
00:16:04,213 --> 00:16:05,756
I said something
I shouldn't have

337
00:16:05,840 --> 00:16:07,175
that upset you, is that it?

338
00:16:07,967 --> 00:16:10,636
[SATOKO] It's fine.
Let me sleep.

339
00:16:10,720 --> 00:16:13,598
Satoko, I love you.

340
00:16:16,476 --> 00:16:19,020
We are still going
to get married, aren't we?

341
00:16:21,147 --> 00:16:22,273
[SATOKO] Maybe.

342
00:16:22,982 --> 00:16:24,275
[Shinpei breathes shakily]

343
00:16:25,276 --> 00:16:27,195
What do you mean by that?

344
00:16:27,278 --> 00:16:29,614
Were you lying about wanting
to marry me?

345
00:16:30,781 --> 00:16:32,742
Do I have to remind you?

346
00:16:33,868 --> 00:16:35,578
If you break your promise,

347
00:16:35,661 --> 00:16:37,830
there's no reason either of us
should keep--

348
00:16:37,914 --> 00:16:40,041
I said I'm going to sleep now.

349
00:16:43,878 --> 00:16:46,797
[SATOKO]
Oh, what am I thinking?

350
00:16:46,881 --> 00:16:49,133
He didn't even
do anything wrong.

351
00:16:50,259 --> 00:16:52,345
But for some reason, I'm angry.

352
00:16:52,428 --> 00:16:55,181
No, it's more than that.
I'm furious with him.

353
00:16:55,264 --> 00:16:58,267
What is wrong with me?

354
00:17:02,813 --> 00:17:04,190
[groans]

355
00:17:04,273 --> 00:17:05,274
[sighs]

356
00:17:05,775 --> 00:17:07,235
[SATOKO] I feel much better.

357
00:17:07,318 --> 00:17:08,277
[door slides open]

358
00:17:08,361 --> 00:17:09,570
-[SHINPEI] Satoko?
-[gasps]

359
00:17:10,780 --> 00:17:11,989
Listen, I've got some

360
00:17:12,073 --> 00:17:13,491
really good news
for you this morning.

361
00:17:13,574 --> 00:17:15,993
-Huh?
-Guess what?

362
00:17:16,077 --> 00:17:17,995
I managed to secure us a ship.

363
00:17:18,079 --> 00:17:20,081
We're getting off the island
safely.

364
00:17:20,164 --> 00:17:21,207
What?

365
00:17:21,290 --> 00:17:23,084
I had to slip a bribe
to a captain.

366
00:17:23,584 --> 00:17:25,628
Though, I'm afraid
we won't leave for 10 days.

367
00:17:25,711 --> 00:17:26,629
You mean it?

368
00:17:26,712 --> 00:17:28,172
Was it really that easy?

369
00:17:28,256 --> 00:17:30,341
"Easy" is not how
I'd describe it.

370
00:17:30,424 --> 00:17:32,969
Took me days of negotiation
to convince him.

371
00:17:33,719 --> 00:17:34,971
[SATOKO]
He said being bought out

372
00:17:35,054 --> 00:17:37,139
was the only way off the island.

373
00:17:37,223 --> 00:17:38,641
Is this really safe?

374
00:17:40,309 --> 00:17:43,396
No, any method will come
with its risks.

375
00:17:43,479 --> 00:17:45,606
I should celebrate the chance.

376
00:17:45,690 --> 00:17:47,400
Thank you for the effort.

377
00:17:47,483 --> 00:17:49,235
It's dangerous outside,

378
00:17:49,318 --> 00:17:51,404
so we can spend
the 10 days here.

379
00:17:51,487 --> 00:17:54,282
A woman outside of a brothel
would draw attention.

380
00:17:54,907 --> 00:17:56,951
I'll be right back
with some food for us.

381
00:17:57,034 --> 00:17:58,869
Oh, let me go with you.

382
00:17:58,953 --> 00:18:00,079
There's no need.

383
00:18:00,162 --> 00:18:01,956
Just get your rest
so you'll feel better.

384
00:18:02,748 --> 00:18:04,542
You can lean on me a bit more.

385
00:18:05,084 --> 00:18:06,335
[Satoko gasps softly]

386
00:18:06,419 --> 00:18:07,420
[door slides open]

387
00:18:07,503 --> 00:18:09,088
♪

388
00:18:09,171 --> 00:18:10,756
[footsteps receding]

389
00:18:11,757 --> 00:18:13,926
[SATOKO]
He's acting the same as ever.

390
00:18:14,010 --> 00:18:16,053
Was I just being too sensitive?

391
00:18:17,847 --> 00:18:21,225
I can't have this sort of
relationship with an assassin.

392
00:18:22,018 --> 00:18:23,644
I should go out there
and apologize

393
00:18:23,728 --> 00:18:25,313
for my behavior yesterday.

394
00:18:26,689 --> 00:18:27,940
[PROSTITUTE 1] Ah, Lord Shinpei!

395
00:18:28,024 --> 00:18:29,692
[PROSTITUTE 2]
It's been far too long!

396
00:18:29,775 --> 00:18:31,610
[PROSTITUTE 3] What a treat
to see Lord Shinpei

397
00:18:31,694 --> 00:18:33,237
first thing in the morning
like this!

398
00:18:33,321 --> 00:18:34,822
[PROSTITUTE 1] My lord,
you're as handsome as ever.

399
00:18:34,905 --> 00:18:35,823
[PROSTITUTE 2]
Thank you for gracing us.

400
00:18:35,906 --> 00:18:37,742
[all giggling]

401
00:18:37,825 --> 00:18:40,995
Oh, Satoko, look!
I've got your food right...

402
00:18:41,620 --> 00:18:42,747
here?

403
00:18:43,706 --> 00:18:45,916
I only came out
to go to the privy.

404
00:18:45,999 --> 00:18:47,126
[all gasp]

405
00:18:47,710 --> 00:18:51,297
[SHINPEI] Uh...
but the privy's the other way!

406
00:18:53,466 --> 00:18:55,509
[AOI]
A pleasure to meet you, Satoko.

407
00:18:55,593 --> 00:18:57,011
My name is Aoi.

408
00:18:57,094 --> 00:18:58,763
I've been assigned
as your instructor here

409
00:18:58,846 --> 00:19:00,097
for the time being.

410
00:19:00,181 --> 00:19:02,016
Please feel free
to ask me anything.

411
00:19:02,099 --> 00:19:03,934
[SATOKO]
I look forward to learning.

412
00:19:04,018 --> 00:19:06,103
Why bother making yourself work?

413
00:19:06,187 --> 00:19:07,730
If they're going
to put me up here,

414
00:19:07,813 --> 00:19:09,231
I won't allow it to be for free.

415
00:19:09,857 --> 00:19:11,150
[Shinpei groans softly]

416
00:19:11,233 --> 00:19:13,486
Keep it to light jobs at least.

417
00:19:13,569 --> 00:19:14,820
[Satoko exclaims]

418
00:19:14,904 --> 00:19:17,323
I spoke to him
too harshly again.

419
00:19:17,406 --> 00:19:20,409
Pardon, but may I ask
what your relationship is

420
00:19:20,493 --> 00:19:22,161
-with Lord Shinpei?
-What?

421
00:19:22,244 --> 00:19:25,122
There are rumors going around
about the two of you.

422
00:19:25,206 --> 00:19:26,707
Lord Shinpei rarely visits,

423
00:19:26,791 --> 00:19:29,543
but suddenly, he brings a beauty
and stays for days on end.

424
00:19:29,627 --> 00:19:32,213
No, there is nothing between us.

425
00:19:32,296 --> 00:19:34,757
He simply connected me
to this brothel for work.

426
00:19:34,840 --> 00:19:37,218
Oh, really?
That's not how it seems to me.

427
00:19:37,301 --> 00:19:38,719
-Uh?
-After you collapsed,

428
00:19:38,803 --> 00:19:40,346
he was so worried
he couldn't sleep.

429
00:19:40,429 --> 00:19:43,015
He stayed up all night
tending to you.

430
00:19:43,641 --> 00:19:44,767
[Satoko exhales softly]

431
00:19:45,476 --> 00:19:49,230
I, uh... I have a question
I'd like to ask you.

432
00:19:49,313 --> 00:19:51,857
Everyone knows the name
Shinpei Goto,

433
00:19:51,941 --> 00:19:54,360
but what do the people here
actually think of him?

434
00:19:54,443 --> 00:19:56,153
You mean you really don't know?

435
00:19:57,321 --> 00:19:58,447
Throughout the island,

436
00:19:58,781 --> 00:20:02,076
he serves as bodyguard
for every brothel you'll find.

437
00:20:02,827 --> 00:20:05,204
Any time there's
a troublesome customer,

438
00:20:05,287 --> 00:20:07,540
he puts them in their place
to protect us.

439
00:20:07,623 --> 00:20:11,085
Naturally, many of the ladies
have come to deeply admire him.

440
00:20:11,168 --> 00:20:13,754
Even the brothel owners
appreciate his work

441
00:20:13,838 --> 00:20:16,799
and show their respect.
He's a marvel around here.

442
00:20:17,758 --> 00:20:19,051
[SATOKO] As I thought,

443
00:20:19,135 --> 00:20:22,096
no one knows the truth,
that he's an assassin.

444
00:20:22,179 --> 00:20:24,056
But I've heard
something curious.

445
00:20:24,140 --> 00:20:26,725
Apparently, Lord Shinpei
is not one to grow attached

446
00:20:26,809 --> 00:20:28,561
to any courtesan in particular.

447
00:20:28,644 --> 00:20:29,645
[SAWARABI] Oh, my!

448
00:20:29,728 --> 00:20:31,480
What are you dressed
like that for?

449
00:20:31,564 --> 00:20:32,523
[BOTH] Mm?

450
00:20:33,023 --> 00:20:35,151
[HATSUNE] Have you given up
on finding customers?

451
00:20:35,234 --> 00:20:38,404
Though I must say,
you had bad luck the other day.

452
00:20:38,487 --> 00:20:40,239
Did I hear the rumors correctly?

453
00:20:40,322 --> 00:20:42,867
Someone served Lord Nitobe sake
instead of water?

454
00:20:42,950 --> 00:20:45,744
Who would ever do
such a terrible thing like that?

455
00:20:45,828 --> 00:20:47,371
[footsteps]

456
00:20:48,539 --> 00:20:50,999
Are you feeling healthy again?

457
00:20:51,083 --> 00:20:53,502
Yes, I am.
I'm sorry to have troubled you.

458
00:20:53,586 --> 00:20:56,338
Oh, how nice
to have Lord Shinpei

459
00:20:56,422 --> 00:20:58,132
nursing you back to health.

460
00:20:58,215 --> 00:21:01,510
I wish that I had been born
as sickly as you.

461
00:21:01,594 --> 00:21:03,721
I find that remark
in poor taste...

462
00:21:04,513 --> 00:21:06,056
You need to learn your place

463
00:21:06,140 --> 00:21:08,434
and stop getting clever with us,
new girl.

464
00:21:08,517 --> 00:21:11,771
And don't you dare
get any closer to Lord Shinpei.

465
00:21:12,354 --> 00:21:14,523
There's only one
he favors around here.

466
00:21:14,607 --> 00:21:16,734
That's Yukari. You understand?

467
00:21:16,817 --> 00:21:17,860
What?

468
00:21:18,319 --> 00:21:19,820
[smirks]

469
00:21:20,404 --> 00:21:21,781
♪

470
00:21:24,909 --> 00:21:28,204
[♪ closing theme song playing]

